NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: Mostly NAMING. "Failure-foreshadowing signature / cheap early-warning monitor" is a relabel of the well-trodden 'score the partial trajectory online to predict the outcome' family (AgentBoard progress-rate, step-level PRMs, agent runtime monitors). The genuine MECHANISM/protocol delta is narrow: a cheap stdlib heuristic (EWMA tool-error + n-gram looping + info-gain decline) plus a MEASURED lead-time-vs-agent's-own-termination and a head-to-head that must beat self-confidence AND difficulty. That delta is an evaluation-protocol contribution, not a new mechanism — and its load-bearing half (beats self-confidence) is ALREADY FALSIFIED at L0 (AUC delta -0.006, CI [-0.011,-0.001]). What survives ('distinct from difficulty + ~2.3-step lead time') is precisely the part most covered by progress-rate/PRM prior art, so the survivor is the LEAST novel half.

FATAL_COLLISIONS: NONE VERIFIED (egress blocked; cannot meet the ≥2-independent-source bar for a kill). Candidate collisions to verify: (1) AgentBoard progress-rate vs the 'distinct-from-difficulty online progression' weak form; (2) step-level PRMs vs claim (c) 'online monitor predicts eventual failure from partial trajectory'. If either is confirmed online-and-predictive, the surviving weak form is a relabeling and warrants RED.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK: [
  "AgentBoard (Ma 2024) — must position lead-time/early-warning against progress-rate explicitly",
  "Step-level / Process Reward Models for agent trajectories — must distinguish cheap-heuristic monitor from trained PRM and show the lead-time/early-warning delta",
  "Automated Failure Attribution (Zhang ICML 2025) — online vs post-hoc framing",
  "LLM confidence calibration line (Kadavath 2022; Xiong 2024; Tian 2023) — required to justify the L1 self-confidence-flip hypothesis"
]

RATIONALE: The strong claim is already dead at L0 (does not beat self-confidence), so the only novelty left to defend is the weak form, which sits squarely on top of published online-progress / PRM scoring — the most-trodden ground, not the freshest. The truly novel, undefeated hook is conditional: does a cheap monitor beat REAL miscalibrated self-confidence on real traces (the L1 question)? That is not settled by prior art and would be a real delta IF demonstrated, but it is currently a hypothesis, not a result. I cannot cast RED because the fatal collisions (AgentBoard/PRM) could not be live-verified to the ≥2-source standard this session (web-search egress blocked). I cannot cast GREEN because the surviving contribution is thin and overlaps named prior art. Honest YELLOW. SCOPING FIX TO CLEAR: a real ≥2-source sweep confirming (a) no existing online agent-trajectory scorer already reports lead-time-vs-agent-termination AND (b) none already does the matched-flag-rate head-to-head vs self-confidence; plus an L1 on real traces with real miscalibrated self-confidence to test the flip. Sources cited above are from training knowledge and were NOT retrievable/verified in this session.
